socket2 0.6.5: TCP keep-alive idle time on QNX 8

socket2 imports libc::TCP_KEEPIDLE for QNX 8, but libc 0.2.186 (the last
release that knows target_env "nto80", see the recipe) does not define it:
"unresolved import libc::TCP_KEEPIDLE". Define it with QNX 8's value (256,
<netinet/tcp.h>) and, as QNX 8's io-sock is the FreeBSD stack, set it in
seconds like the BSDs; the struct timeval form stays for QNX 7 (nto70/71),
whose TCP_KEEPALIVE takes one.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [libc crate gap for target_env nto80]
